{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CftPbjRjLGHt2KxBZFxrZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need a concise 3-step strategy for figuring out which peer is most reliable given file-based messaging with one-hour lifespans. The constraints point toward designing verifiable tasks to establish ground truth, accounting for limited sample size and polling/race condition issues, then tracking results over repeated trials to build confidence in reliability scores.\n\nFirst, send canary tasks with known answers to each peer and log latency/correctness with atomic file writes. Second, score peers using a confidence-adjusted accuracy measure that favors larger sample sizes, routing most work to the top scorer while keeping a small exploration slice. Third, continuously verify high-stakes outputs and freeze/record the ranking near the hour's end so the conclusion persists — keeping each bullet tight while noting the core trade-offs like canary cost versus learning speed and the risk of peers gaming known test patterns.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3666,"cache_read_input_tokens":12686,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3666},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3dd92cee-70cf-4e1a-b36a-94014c1ada1f","uuid":"104e3286-3e57-4b9b-b21d-0c2ff8b067a4","timestamp":"2026-10-10T10:22:13.118Z","request_id":"req_011CftPbj1vGGevrtU52KDyo","thinking_duration_ms":7933,"thinking_display":"summarized"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CftPbjRjLGHt2KxBZFxrZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"- **Seed with canary tasks (first ~10 min):** Send every peer the same small set of tasks with known answers, mixed in with real work so they can't tell them apart. Log each response's correctness and latency to a ledger file, written to a temp file and renamed into place so readers never see a partial write. Costs some tokens up front, but it is the only way to get ground truth in one hour.\n- **Score conservatively and route with exploration (next ~35 min):** Score each peer by a lower confidence bound on its accuracy, such as Beta(1,1) plus a timeout penalty, so a peer that is 2/2 doesn't outrank one that is 18/20. Send most real work to the top scorer, but keep 10–20% going to the others to catch degradation and avoid locking in on early luck. Small samples are the main risk, so a wide interval should mean \"keep exploring,\" not \"pick it.\"\n- **Cross-check high-stakes outputs and freeze a handoff (last ~15 min):** For results that matter, get a second peer's answer and compare, rather than trusting self-reported confidence, which is unreliable. At about 50 minutes, stop routing new work, write the final ranking with its sample sizes and uncertainty to a handoff file, and note which conclusions rest on too few samples to trust. The handoff file is what outlives the agent, so the conclusion has to be written down before the lifespan ends."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3666,"cache_read_input_tokens":12686,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3666},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3dd92cee-70cf-4e1a-b36a-9